From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: PS5: say where the server's time goes.

In a Steam start on the Pro (2026-11-22, docs/STEAM.md) the callers of create_file waited 17 ms a call on average,
113 ms in the worst 10 s, and every other request slowed with it: 183 of the 461 seconds threads spent in server
calls. The callers' waits are all that is recorded, so nothing said whether the server worked in the request, listed
watched directories (patches 0902 and 2091) or did not run.

While requests come the server now writes one line every 10 s to standard error, the Wine log:

  wineserver: times ms= wakes= polled= loop_ms= loop_cpu_ms= requests= request_ms= direct= direct_ms=
      lock_waits= lock_wait_ms= change_lists= change_ms= change_items= top name=calls/average us/longest us ...

loop_ms is the wall time the main loop held the lock between two sleeps and loop_cpu_ms its thread's CPU time in
them (the difference is time blocked in a system call or not running); polled counts wakes of the poll() fallback;
direct are the requests client threads ran themselves (patch 0918) and lock_wait what they slept for the lock;
change_* the lists of watched directories, timer and kqueue alike; top the eight requests with the most time in
their handlers. Two clock reads a request and four a wake; nothing is formatted except that line.
---
 server/change.c  |  12 +++++-
 server/fd.c      |  16 +++++++
 server/request.c | 125 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 server/trace.c   |   7 ++++
 4 files changed, 159 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/change.c b/server/change.c
index 26c701d..cbf0dd8 100644
--- a/server/change.c
+++ b/server/change.c
@@ -1321,6 +1321,10 @@ static void poll_timeout( void *private )
     watch->count = count;
     /* a listing that takes long is made less often: eight times as long between two */
     took = ((long long)(after.tv_sec - before.tv_sec) * 1000000000 + (after.tv_nsec - before.tv_nsec)) / 100;
+    {
+        extern void ps5_times_change( unsigned long long ns, unsigned int items );
+        ps5_times_change( took * 100, count );
+    }
     watch->interval = took * 8 < POLL_MIN_INTERVAL ? POLL_MIN_INTERVAL
                       : took * 8 > POLL_MAX_INTERVAL ? POLL_MAX_INTERVAL : took * 8;
     poll_arm( dir );
@@ -1407,7 +1411,13 @@ static int inotify_adjust_changes( struct dir *dir )
     watch->vnode = -1;
     vnode_add( dir );   /* before the first list, so that no change falls between the two */
     /* the list the next ones are compared with is made now, before the caller can change anything */
-    poll_scan( base, "", dir->subtree, 0, &watch->items, &watch->count, &size );
+    {
+        extern unsigned long long ps5_times_now( int cpu );
+        extern void ps5_times_change( unsigned long long ns, unsigned int items );
+        unsigned long long started = ps5_times_now( 0 );
+        poll_scan( base, "", dir->subtree, 0, &watch->items, &watch->count, &size );
+        ps5_times_change( ps5_times_now( 0 ) - started, watch->count );
+    }
     if (watch->items) qsort( watch->items, watch->count, sizeof(*watch->items), poll_compare );
     poll_arm( dir );
     return 1;
diff --git a/server/fd.c b/server/fd.c
index fc9ba34..097c09a 100644
--- a/server/fd.c
+++ b/server/fd.c
@@ -364,6 +364,10 @@ static const timeout_t user_shared_data_timeout = 16 * 10000;
  * pw_wineserver_call_direct, request.c) under this lock, which the server
  * thread holds except while it sleeps in kqueue/epoll. */
 pthread_mutex_t inprocess_server_mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+extern void ps5_times_loop_wake( int polled );   /* request.c: where the server's time goes */
+extern void ps5_times_loop_sleep(void);
+#endif
